# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages reads this file from the root of what it publishes. For Rubric Print that is
# `app/` — set as the build output directory, with no build command — which is also
# what keeps `data/` and `tools/` off the public site. Pages consumes this file and
# never serves it. Syntax is a path pattern on its own line with its headers indented
# under it; a line beginning with # is a comment.
#
# WHY ONLY THESE. Everything else is precached by sw.js and answered out of Cache
# Storage, which ignores Cache-Control entirely. What is pinned here is the update
# path, and nothing else needs to be.
#
#   sw.js  — CACHE in sw.js is bumped by hand on every deploy that changes the shell,
#            and `activate` then deletes every cache that is not the new one. None of
#            that starts until the browser fetches a sw.js it has not seen before, so
#            a worker served from an HTTP cache is a teacher opening last week's app
#            with the bump discipline intact and useless.
#
#   the shell document — pinned for the loads that happen before there is a service
#            worker at all: the first visit, and the first one after site data is
#            cleared, which takes the worker with it. BOTH paths are listed because a
#            teacher types the bare origin, so the request carrying the shell arrives
#            at `/`, and a rule written for `/index.html` does not match it.
#
# no-cache is not no-store: the browser still keeps the copy and revalidates, so a
# deploy that changed nothing costs a 304 rather than a download.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT THE WHOLE STORY, and the part it cannot say is the part that bit
# Planbook first. A Cloudflare zone has its own Browser Cache TTL, four hours by
# default on a new zone, and it REWRITES Cache-Control on anything the edge caches —
# which includes .js. Planbook's first deploy served /sw.js as max-age=14400 with a
# correct _headers file in place. HTML escaped it only because the edge does not cache
# HTML by default. The zone must be set to **Respect Existing Headers**
# (Caching → Configuration) or nothing here binds. Re-read /sw.js on the wire after
# any zone change: a green file in the repo proves nothing about what a browser was
# told.

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
